WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.305 --> 00:00:16.335
"Oh Maggie cried.

2
00:00:16.355 --> 00:00:18.697
"Did that van run over our bikes?"

3
00:00:19.758 --> 00:00:20.599
"I don't think so."

4
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:22.621
Cole hurried over to the bikes.

5
00:00:24.402 --> 00:00:26.584
"Here's yours, Maggie," he said, picking it up.

6
00:00:26.604 --> 00:00:28.185
"It looks okay."

7
00:00:30.027 --> 00:00:31.348
Henry picked up another bike.

8
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.401
"I think they're okay.

9
00:00:34.421 --> 00:00:38.023
It looks like someone just threw them into the street behind the van."

10
00:00:38.043 --> 00:00:39.744
"Oh my!"

11
00:00:40.084 --> 00:00:41.385
Mr. Moss looked alarmed.

12
00:00:41.405 --> 00:00:44.947
"Are you sure it wasn't an accident?

13
00:00:46.068 --> 00:00:48.969
I can't imagine anyone in Belltown wanting to harm your bikes."

14
00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.432
Before becoming a detective, Henry couldn't have imagined it either.

15
00:00:54.312 --> 00:00:55.533
Now he wasn't so sure.

16
00:00:55.553 --> 00:00:59.175
"Did you see anything suspicious while we were inside?"

17
00:00:59.455 --> 00:01:00.196
he asked Mr.

18
00:01:00.236 --> 00:01:03.401
Moss. "I'm afraid not," Mr.

19
00:01:03.441 --> 00:01:04.162
Moss replied.

20
00:01:04.182 --> 00:01:07.264
"Shortly after you went in, I ran out of paint.

21
00:01:08.305 --> 00:01:10.746
I walked over to Belltown Hardware to buy more."

22
00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:16.411
"Maybe those little kids knocked the bikes over on their way into the Sweet Shop," Cole suggested.

23
00:01:16.431 --> 00:01:18.752
"They seemed awfully excited."

24
00:01:19.693 --> 00:01:23.115
"They might have knocked them down by accident, I guess," Maggie said.

25
00:01:23.135 --> 00:01:26.918
"But how did our bikes end up in the street behind the van?"

26
00:01:27.158 --> 00:01:27.719
she asked.

27
00:01:28.639 --> 00:01:29.200
"Never mind."

28
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.022
Henry got on his bike and rode in a circle, testing the steering and brakes.

29
00:01:36.023 --> 00:01:37.303
Everything seemed to be working.

30
00:01:37.323 --> 00:01:40.885
"We should get going," he told Cole and Maggie.

31
00:01:42.486 --> 00:01:43.527
They said good-bye to Mr.

32
00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.488
Moss and rode toward West Belltown.

33
00:01:45.508 --> 00:01:49.170
"Do you think someone messed with our bikes on purpose?"

34
00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:50.270
Cole asked.

35
00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:52.872
"Maybe," Henry said.

36
00:01:52.892 --> 00:01:57.835
"Someone might be trying to send us a message to stop our investigation."

37
00:01:58.915 --> 00:01:59.936
Cole looked skeptical.

38
00:02:00.736 --> 00:02:01.857
"That doesn't make sense.

39
00:02:02.357 --> 00:02:03.438
Who would want to stop us?

40
00:02:04.738 --> 00:02:08.020
Besides, nobody even knew we were at the Sweet Shop just now!"

41
00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.222
"Mr. Tate did," Maggie pointed out.

42
00:02:11.242 --> 00:02:15.824
"Maybe he figured out we were getting suspicious of him and he's trying to frame Mrs.

43
00:02:15.844 --> 00:02:16.485
Sweet again!

44
00:02:17.445 --> 00:02:20.587
He could have followed us to town and messed with our bikes while we were in the Sweet

45
00:02:20.627 --> 00:02:25.390
Shop. Patty was too busy with those kids to look outside and notice anything.

46
00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:28.891
We were in the back of the shop, so we wouldn't have seen Mr.

47
00:02:28.912 --> 00:02:31.008
Tate." "And Mr.

48
00:02:31.088 --> 00:02:34.750
Moss was getting paint, so he wouldn't have seen Mr.

49
00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:35.370
Tate either."

50
00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:36.991
Cole looked skeptical.

51
00:02:37.011 --> 00:02:39.512
"Do you really think Mr.

52
00:02:39.572 --> 00:02:40.132
Tate did it?"

53
00:02:41.573 --> 00:02:46.135
"I guess it's possible—if he's the one who stole the flavor," Henry said.

54
00:02:46.155 --> 00:02:48.076
"We need to find out."

55
00:02:51.597 --> 00:02:54.999
When they reached the Dessert Den, an electrician's truck was parked outside.

56
00:02:55.959 --> 00:02:57.640
The electrician was inside with Mr.

57
00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:02.477
Tate. "Hi, kids," Mr.

58
00:03:02.497 --> 00:03:04.258
Tate said when Cole knocked on the door.

59
00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:08.281
He glanced at the electrician who was working on an overhead light.

60
00:03:08.301 --> 00:03:11.323
"I can't talk right now," he told the kids.

61
00:03:11.343 --> 00:03:15.125
"I have to make sure the lights are ready in time for my grand opening.

62
00:03:15.966 --> 00:03:16.887
Can you come back later?"

63
00:03:16.907 --> 00:03:19.829
"Sure, I guess," Cole said.

64
00:03:19.849 --> 00:03:23.451
"Now what?"

65
00:03:23.871 --> 00:03:25.612
Maggie said as the door shut behind them.

66
00:03:27.093 --> 00:03:30.636
They could see some neighborhood kids running around in a lot a short distance away.

67
00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.361
"Let's go see if Robby is over there," Cole suggested.

68
00:03:34.381 --> 00:03:36.942
"He's one of our suspects, remember?"

69
00:03:43.503 --> 00:03:45.444
Robby?" Henry asked the other kids.

70
00:03:46.624 --> 00:03:47.324
Emma shrugged.

71
00:03:47.344 --> 00:03:49.825
"He took off on his bike a while ago.

72
00:03:50.365 --> 00:03:51.306
I don't know where he went."

73
00:03:51.326 --> 00:03:55.047
"Have you guys seen the menu inside the Dessert Den?"

74
00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:56.067
Maggie blurted out.

75
00:03:56.087 --> 00:03:57.487
"When did Mr.

76
00:03:57.527 --> 00:03:58.047
Tate get it?"

77
00:03:59.008 --> 00:03:59.728
A kid shrugged.

78
00:04:00.532 --> 00:04:03.053
"I peeked in there once, but I didn't notice a sign."

79
00:04:03.073 --> 00:04:05.114
"When did you peek in?"

80
00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:06.074
Maggie asked.

81
00:04:06.775 --> 00:04:08.695
"Was it before or after Monday morning?"

82
00:04:10.096 --> 00:04:11.277
The kid looked surprised.

83
00:04:11.297 --> 00:04:12.777
"I don't remember.

84
00:04:13.197 --> 00:04:15.999
Why?" "No reason," Cole said.

85
00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:18.259
"But have any of you noticed Mr.

86
00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.841
Tate doing anything weird during the past few days?"

87
00:04:20.861 --> 00:04:23.422
"Wait," someone said.

88
00:04:23.442 --> 00:04:25.643
"I thought you guys were working for Mr.

89
00:04:25.663 --> 00:04:28.824
Tate. Now it sounds like you're investigating him!"

90
00:04:30.024 --> 00:04:30.984
Emma's face lit up.

91
00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:33.325
"If you're trying to prove Mr.

92
00:04:33.345 --> 00:04:35.986
Tate did something wrong, I bet my parents would help you!

93
00:04:36.486 --> 00:04:37.286
Robby's too."

94
00:04:37.306 --> 00:04:39.007
"They would?

95
00:04:39.607 --> 00:04:40.867
Why?" Henry asked.

96
00:04:40.887 --> 00:04:45.328
"Our parents were upset when they found out about the Dessert Den," Emma said.

97
00:04:45.348 --> 00:04:50.370
"They were getting ready to ask the town council if they could start a community garden in some

98
00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:51.310
of the empty lots."

99
00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.971
"Really?" Cole said, shooting a look at Henry.

100
00:04:56.091 --> 00:04:58.112
Henry's head was already spinning with thoughts.

101
00:04:59.084 --> 00:05:00.425
Could Emma's news be a clue?

102
00:05:01.406 --> 00:05:04.828
It sounded as if some people in the neighborhood had a motive for harming Mr.

103
00:05:04.848 --> 00:05:05.568
Tate's business.

104
00:05:07.129 --> 00:05:10.992
Still, Henry couldn't imagine a bunch of adults stealing an ice-cream flavor.

105
00:05:12.073 --> 00:05:14.094
Especially if they knew it would get nice Mrs.

106
00:05:14.134 --> 00:05:14.855
Sweet in trouble.

107
00:05:14.875 --> 00:05:17.436
"Have any of you seen Mrs.

108
00:05:17.516 --> 00:05:19.398
Sweet hanging around here lately?"

109
00:05:19.698 --> 00:05:20.218
he asked.

110
00:05:21.559 --> 00:05:22.920
Most of the kids shook their heads.

111
00:05:24.961 --> 00:05:26.442
But a girl named Hannah smirked.

112
00:05:26.462 --> 00:05:28.083
"Are you kidding?"

113
00:05:28.443 --> 00:05:28.884
she said.

114
00:05:29.769 --> 00:05:33.378
"Mrs. Sweet doesn't have time to hang around West Belltown these days.

115
00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.646
She's too busy going out on dates with Mr.

116
00:05:36.686 --> 00:05:37.187
Moss!"
